      <div type="clause" n="43">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 43</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="43" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="108" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXXVII. Ðonne mon beam on wuda forbærne, ⁊ weorðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_43.lnote.oe.5-3"/> yppe on þone ðe hit dyde, gielde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_43.lnote.oe.6-3"/> he fulwite: geselle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_43.lnote.oe.7-2"/> LX scill.; forþamþe fýr bið þeof.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="43" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="108" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXXVII. Ðonne man beam on wuda forbærne, ⁊ wurðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_43.lnote.oe.3"/> yppe on þone þe hit dyde, gilde he fulwite<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_43.lnote.oe.4-2"/>: ⁊ gesylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_43.lnote.oe.5-2"/> LX scll'; forðonðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_43.lnote.oe.6-2"/> fyr bið þeof.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="43" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="108" ed="#liebermann"/>Be wude bærnete. Ðonne mon beam on wuda forbærne, ⁊ wyrðe yppe on ðone ðe hit dyde, gylde he fulwite<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_43.lnote.oe.1"/>: gesylle syxtig scill'; forðamðe fyr bið ðeof.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="43" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="109" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis in nemore trabem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_43.lnote.oe.4"/> combusserit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_43.lnote.oe.5"/>, et notum denique<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_43.lnote.oe.6"/> fuerit in actore<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_43.lnote.oe.7"/>, soluat plenam witam et emendet LX sol.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_43.lnote.oe.8"/>, quia ignis est<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_43.lnote.oe.9"/> fur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="50" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be wude bærnete.] Ðonne mon beam on wuda forbærne, ⁊ weorðe yppe on þone ðe hit dyde, gielde he fulwite: geselle<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#Ine_43.attnote.fn.8"/> LX scill., forþamþe<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#Ine_43.attnote.fn.9"/> fýr bið þeof.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="44" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="408" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LXXXVII} Ðonne mon beam on wuda forbærne, ⁊ weorðe yppe on þone ðe hit dyde, gielde he fulwite: geselle LX sciƚƚ, forþamþe fyr bið þeof.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="109" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand einen Baum im Walde verbrennt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_43.lnote.de.1"/>, und es wird [dem Richter] kund über den, der es gethan hat, so zahle dieser volles Strafgeld<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_43.lnote.de.2"/>: er gebe 60 Schill.; weil Feuer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_43.lnote.de.3"/> ein Dieb ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone burns a tree in the wood, and it becomes known [to the judge] who did it, let him pay the full fine: let him give 60 shillings; because fire is a thief.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="51" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone destroys a tree in a wood by fire, and it becomes known who did it, he shall pay a full fine. He shall pay 60 shillings, because fire is a thief.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="404" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone burns down a tree in the wood, and it is disclosed who did it, he is to pay full fine; he is to pay 60 shillings, for fire is a thief.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="409" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>When someone burns a tree in the forest, and it becomes known who did it, let him pay a full fine; let him pay 60 shillings because “fire is a thief.”</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="278"><label>contradicts</label> <ref target="clause:Af_9-2">Af 9.2</ref> <quote>where Ine called sixty shillings the 'full fine' with evident reference to theft, Alfred stipulated that 120 shillings was to be the fine for all thefts (n. 72)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="299"><label>emends</label> <ref target="clause:Af_12">Af 12</ref> <quote>Ine §44 stipulates that a man must pay 30 shillings for each of the first three trees [...] Alfred §14 requires only a 5-shilling payment</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="305"><label>?Alfredian penalty; contrast Ine</label> <ref target="clause:IIAs_1">II As 1–1.5</ref> <quote>enforce the (?Alfredian) penalty of 120 shillings on those convicted by due process; Ine had merely forbidden vendetta for thieves killed in flagrante, and his penalty for others seems to have been 60 shillings</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> fullw.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to fullw.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">109</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">109</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">percusserit <hi rend="italic">R Lond; verbessert</hi> combusserit <hi rend="italic">Co Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">percusserit R Lond; corrected to combusserit Co Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">109</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">f. d. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">f. d. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">109</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">auct. <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">auct. T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">109</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt M</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in M</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">109</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">f. e. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">f. e. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> fullw.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to fullw.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> -ðamðe</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to -ðamðe</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.oe.5-3" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wyrþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wyrþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.oe.6-3" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gylde <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gylde Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">⁊ gesylle syxtig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">⁊ gesylle syxtig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Baum 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Baum 4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Strafgeldfixum 12. i. — H Ld Q setzen fälschlich ‘und’ ein; daher meint Schreuer, dass neben Strafe 60 Schill. Busse für jeden Baum entfalle: laut Af 12 unmöglich hoch. Vielmehr will das ‘weil’ erklären, wieso ‘<hi rend="spaced">volle</hi> Strafe’ eintritt; es wäre sinnlos, wenn 60 Schill. dem Geschädigten zuflössen. Ine spricht vom Fiskus allein; Kläger erhält wohl Doppelersatz hier wie 43, 1. 44</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See Gl</hi> Strafgeldfixum 12. i. — H Ld Q wrongly insert ‘and’; hence Schreuer thinks that, besides the fine, 60 shill. compensation is due for each tree: impossibly high in view of Af 12. Rather, the ‘because’ is meant to explain why the <hi rend="italic">full</hi> fine is incurred; it would be meaningless if 60 shill. went to the injured party. Ine speaks of the fisc alone; the plaintiff probably receives double compensation here, as in 43, 1. 44</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_43.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> heimlich 2; Sprichwörter 2. Die Graugans schilt Dieb den, der den Stumpf des gefällten Baumes verdeckt; Wilda 863</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> heimlich 2; Sprichwörter 2. The Grágás calls a thief the man who covers up the stump of the felled tree; Wilda 863</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_43.attnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">50</biblScope></bibl><label>geselle</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">⁊ gesylle</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_43.attnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">50</biblScope></bibl><label>forþamþe</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">forðonðe</hi>. H.</seg></note>
